6,"Kayah, Western | World Mission Media",https://worldmission.media/languages-of-the-world/kayah-western,"Western Kayah language is a vital part of the Kayah cultural identity, embodying traditional beliefs and practices.A Tibeto-Burman language, part of the Sino-Tibetan family. Spoken in Kayah State, Myanmar, and by small communities in Thailand. Around 26,000 speakers.","Kayah, Western",Sino-Tibetan
7,Kayah (Western) Translation Services | Language Guide | LEXIGO,https://lexigo.com/languages/kayah-western,"Western Kayah, also known as Western Kayah Li, is a Sino-Tibetan language of the Karen branch spoken by approximately 100,000 people, primarily in the western part of Kayah State, Myanmar.","Kayah, Western",Sino-Tibetan
8,Karenni language,https://grokipedia.com/page/Karenni_language,"The Karenni language, also known as Kayah or Red Karen, is a dialect continuum of the Karenic branch within the Sino-Tibetan language family, spoken primarily by the Kayah people in Kayah State and adjacent regions of eastern Myanmar...","Kayah, Western",Sino-Tibetan
